    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n111621" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλτᾰτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, irreg. 
			Sup. of
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλος,</span> mostly poet., <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			6.91
		</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>P.</u>
			9.98
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			A.
			<u>Th.</u>
			16
		</span></i>, Ar.Ach.<i><span class="en">
			885
		</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ φ.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one's nearest and dearest,</i>
			
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλος</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1.1c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					234
				</span></i>
			; less freq. in Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Prt.</u>
				314a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Grg.</u>
				513a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				650a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				4.3.2
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ φ. σώματα,</span> opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ἀλλοτρίους,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Aeschin.
				3.78
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίντατος.</span></div>
